From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:19:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] extmod/modos: keep the input os.dupterm_notify() has no room
 for.

os.dupterm_notify() moves every character a dupterm stream holds into
stdin_ringbuf, and ringbuf_put() drops each one that doesn't fit. On the
esp32 port, WebREPL's socket calls it whenever a poll finds the socket
readable, and that can be right after a timer callback has run inside
the REPL's wait for input. A command that arrived during the callback,
which mpremote and other tools send in one piece, is then cut to what
fits in the buffer plus whatever arrives later: the REPL runs a broken
command, or never sees its Ctrl-D and the tool waits for its timeout.

While the REPL waits for input no interrupt character is set, and
nothing needs the rest read early: mp_hal_stdin_rx_chr() reads the
stream itself once the buffer is empty. So stop when the buffer is full.
While code runs, keep reading as before, so that a Ctrl-C behind a full
buffer still interrupts it.
---
 extmod/modos.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/extmod/modos.c b/extmod/modos.c
index c330162..12bb259 100644
--- a/extmod/modos.c
+++ b/extmod/modos.c
@@ -60,6 +60,10 @@
 #include "genhdr/mpversion.h"
 #endif
 
+#if MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM_NOTIFY
+#include "shared/runtime/interrupt_char.h"
+#endif
+
 #ifdef MICROPY_PY_OS_INCLUDEFILE
 #include MICROPY_PY_OS_INCLUDEFILE
 #endif
@@ -134,6 +138,14 @@ static MP_DEFINE_CONST_FUN_OBJ_0(mp_os_uname_obj, mp_os_uname);
 static mp_obj_t mp_os_dupterm_notify(mp_obj_t obj_in) {
     (void)obj_in;
     for (;;) {
+        // A character read with no room left in stdin_ringbuf is lost. While
+        // the REPL waits for input (no interrupt character is set), leave the
+        // rest in the stream: mp_hal_stdin_rx_chr() reads it from there once
+        // the buffer is empty. While code runs, keep reading so that a Ctrl-C
+        // behind a full buffer still interrupts it.
+        if (mp_interrupt_char < 0 && ringbuf_free(&stdin_ringbuf) == 0) {
+            break;
+        }
         int c = mp_os_dupterm_rx_chr();
         if (c < 0) {
             break;
